     "date": "2026-09-26T21:36:24Z"
    },
    "message": "fix: restore project-local free-port scanning (#125)\n\n* fix(installer): initialize bounded port scans before use\n\nDependent local assignments expanded before start was initialized, so scans returned an occupied port without checking candidates. Split initialization, fail explicitly after 50 occupied candidates, and stop both project-local callers before launcher or registry writes. Preserve each copy's probes and its public containment gate.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* test(installer): cover offline port selection and failure propagation\n\nExercise both real helpers and project-local callers under Bash 3.2-compatible syntax with stubbed probes and effects. Cover all 50 candidates, peer claims, and failures with errexit disabled or suppressed. Keep original source capsules exact through reversible provenance replacements, and refresh the tracked-byte inventory.\n\nCloses #8\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(provenance): generate installer port-scan receipts\n\nCI rebuilds the source ledger before the canonical gates. Declare the reversible port-scan adaptations in the checked-in generator instead of relying on manually maintained output, add a generator-freshness regression, and refresh the tracked-byte receipt.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCopilot-Session: 84ebe30d-3a36-4937-be6b-4103373f9bfe\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: rappter1 <rappter1@icloud.com>\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCopilot-Session: 84ebe30d-3a36-4937-be6b-4103373f9bfe\nCopilot-Session: 3c809e9a-e035-48bc-a028-c6b6de624fbb",
